<title>USA: Springfield, Ill., $27 mln improvement priced.</title>
<headline>Springfield, Ill., $27 mln improvement priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch &amp; Co said Wednesday that it tentatively priced $27 million of Springfield, Ill., combined capital improvement restructuring and new money bond debt, Series 1996C, with a top yield of 5.70 percent in 2021 in the current coupon portion of the offering.</p>
<p>The bonds are MBIA insured.  </p>
